# Code owners for the security-sensitive paths in this repo (#684 / #690).
#
# Why: the CI security gates and their allow-lists must not be widened by
# whoever happens to be editing them. Listing a path here makes GitHub request
# review from its owner automatically on any PR that touches it, and -- once
# branch protection requires it -- hold the merge until that review lands.
#
# WHAT ENFORCES THIS, AND WHAT DOES NOT. Read before treating this as a control:
#   1. This file only requests a reviewer. Blocking a merge additionally needs
#      branch protection on `dev` with "Require review from Code Owners"
#      enabled. That is a repo-admin setting, not a file, and this PR does not
#      and cannot ship it.
#   2. CODEOWNERS is a paid feature for *private* repositories. wcmc-its is on
#      the GitHub Free plan and CViche is private, so as of 2026-09-08 GitHub
#      does not apply this file at all; the branch-protection and ruleset APIs
#      for this repo both answer 403 "Upgrade to GitHub Pro or make this
#      repository public". So this is intent-of-record today. It starts working
#      when the org moves to Team/Enterprise (or the repo goes public) and (1)
#      is turned on.
#
# Owner choice: @mrj4001 is a direct admin collaborator here, so the entry
# resolves. A CODEOWNERS line naming a user or team without write access is
# silently ignored by GitHub -- worse than no file, because it looks like a
# control and is not one. Check before substituting a handle:
#   gh api "repos/wcmc-its/CViche/collaborators?affiliation=direct" --jq '.[].login'
#   gh api repos/wcmc-its/CViche/teams --jq '.[] | [.slug, .permission] | @tsv'
# The only team with repo access today is @wcmc-its/reciter (maintain, 7
# members) -- the application team, not a security team, so it is deliberately
# not used as the owner here. Swap in a dedicated security team once one exists.

# Dependency-vulnerability gate: an entry here suppresses an advisory in CI and
# on the production deploy path alike (buildspec.yaml runs the same pip-audit).
/.pip-audit-ignore.txt      @mrj4001

# Secret-scanning gate: an entry here excludes a path from TruffleHog.
/.trufflehog-exclude.txt    @mrj4001

# CI definitions -- the security gates themselves, and their token permissions.
/.github/workflows/         @mrj4001

# Production build/deploy pipeline (CodeBuild), which carries the deploy-time
# copy of the dependency audit.
/buildspec.yaml             @mrj4001

# This file: ownership rules must not be editable without the same review.
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @mrj4001
